Yiimp Install Scrypt v1.1 // 23.11.2026

Information =>
* Supports Ubuntu Server 22.04 (PHP 8.2) and 24.04 (PHP 8.3)
* PHP version is auto-detected from the OS release; nginx and systemd use the
  matching PHP-FPM version everywhere
* Works with the current Kudaraidee/yiimp repository (default branch "dev")
* SQL dump and ALL follow-up migrations from the yiimp sql/ folder are applied
  automatically, in date order (including 2025-03-31 and the 2025/2026 algo
  updates). Adding a new migration to yiimp no longer requires editing this
  installer.

Fix =>
* Fix broken "printf" typo in output() and several wrong shell redirections
  ("echo ... > sudo tee ...") in the mail/timezone sections
* Fix "sudo apt_install ..." (a shell function cannot be called through sudo)
  when selecting the compiler for stratum
* Build yiimp/stratum as the owning user with gcc-10 wrappers in PATH instead of
  changing the system-wide gcc/g++ alternatives
* Fix git submodule commands that mixed sudo and non-sudo and left root-owned
  files in the user's home directory
* Fix the Ondrej PPA check (the old code looked for a "bionic" file name)
* Fix timezone setup and use certbot instead of the removed "letsencrypt"
  package on Ubuntu 24.04
* Fix MySQL option order (--defaults-file must come first) and use
  CREATE USER/GRANT instead of the deprecated GRANT ... IDENTIFIED BY
* Fix symlink creation so a re-run does not fail with "File exists"
* Remove the fragile "sed -i 14d" on yiimp's defaultconfig.php
* Remove "apt-mark hold openssl" so security updates are not blocked
* Correct the /$HOME/backup path and create /var/bin for yiimp binaries
* Restrict /etc/yiimp/keys.php to root:www-data 0640

Change =>
* install-debug.sh is now a small wrapper that runs install.sh with "bash -x"
  and writes install-debug.log (the old script was for Ubuntu 16.04/18.04)
* Added install-debug.log to .gitignore
* Set default MySQL client credentials in ~/.my.cnf to the yiimp panel user
* Skip Let's Encrypt when the host name is an IP address or no e-mail is given;
  keep the HTTP-only nginx config if certificate issuance fails
* Keep timezone in UTC and start/enable memcached and cron

---
